    {
      "date": "2021-12-11",
      "person_or_event": "Phillips single-lot charity sale, New York",
      "description": "The first 5711/1A-018 sold for $6,503,500 including fees, roughly 124 times its $52,635 retail price, with proceeds to The Nature Conservancy. It closed the 5711 story eleven months after the reference was discontinued.",
      "source_url": "https://www.phillips.com/detail/patek-philippe/NY080121/1T"
    },
    {
      "date": "2021-12-11",
      "person_or_event": "Tiffany 5711 final example auction",
      "description": "The final retail example of the Patek 5711/1A-018 (Tiffany blue) sells at the Phillips New York Watch Auction for $6.5M with premium — the highest auction price ever for a 5711, and a record that tracks the Asian collector market's willingness to pay multiples of MSRP for a final-series piece.",
      "source_url": "https://www.phillips.com/detail/patek-philippe/NY080121/1T"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "story": "Patek's send-off for the 5711 and a nod to 170 years of retail partnership with Tiffany & Co.: 170 pieces with a Tiffany Blue lacquer dial, double-signed on dial and caseback, allocated only through Tiffany boutiques in December 2021. Piece No. 1 went straight to Phillips as a single-lot charity sale and made $6.5 million, the number that came to stand for the entire 2021 watch bubble.",
    "collector_notes": "The dial and caseback double stamp is the whole game; paperwork tracing the Tiffany allocation matters more here than on any standard Nautilus. Later examples have changed hands far below the charity result, which was a one-off number with a philanthropic premium built in.",
    "starter_alternative": "tissot-prx-t137-407"
  },
